      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-116309",
      ":question/problem": "Boyle's law states that when a gas is compressed at a constant temperature, the volume $V$ of the gas, in liters $(L)$, is inversely proportional with the pressure $P$, in kilopascals ($kPa$). If a gas sample has a volume of $90L$ at a pressure of $35kPa$, what is the constant of variation?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
