      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-51985",
      ":question/problem": "The time $t$, in seconds, traveled by a particle varies inversely with its average speed $v$, measured in meters per second ($m/s$). When $v = 2m/s$, the particle travels for $t = 4s$. What is the constant of variation?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
